dialogue.mmo_sawyer.first_words.text = Hm. Calluses on your palms and bark on your boots. You'll do.\nName's Marn. I saw timber. A Kweebec at a sawmill, I know. Somebody's always going to cut it. Might as well be somebody who knows what's inside. Down here in the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color> it's all stone and no trees, so a sawyer's a rare thing, and I keep a mill or two for whoever can feed one. Say hello and we'll talk.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.first_words.opt.hail = Hello, Marn.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.sent_by_guide.text = The Guide sent you down, then. He talks, that one.\nSays you've the look of somebody who could feed a mill. Go on, say it properly and we'll call you introduced.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.sent_by_guide.opt.hail = Hello, Marn.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.menu.text = Marn's still here. Logs don't saw themselves, so say what you need.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trophy_hail.text = Hold on. Show me that.\nThat's a <color is="#ffd97a">Sawmiller's Hatchet</color>. Mithril, balanced at a mill and nowhere else. I've not seen its like in years, and never in a hand this green.\nThe mill hands one of those out about as often as a log splits itself. Keep it sharp.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trophy_hail.opt.show = It came out of the mill.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trophy_talk.text = Still carrying the <color is="#ffd97a">Sawmiller's Hatchet</color>. Good. A blade like that wants working, so don't let it hang on a wall. What do you need?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_offer.text = I've a <b>Sawmill</b> going spare. I don't hand them to just anybody, mind.\nGo chop <b>timber</b>. Cut <b>planks</b> at a Builder's Workbench till you know what a plank costs in sweat, and bring me a share. Do that and the mill's yours.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you planks.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_brief.text = <b>Timber</b> off the tree and <b>planks</b> off a Builder's Workbench. That's the job. The workbench is slow, I know it. That's the point. You'll want the mill all the more for it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_ready.text = Let's see them. <b>Planks</b>, hand-cut, edges all over the place. Good. You'll not cut another one like that once the mill's running. Hand them over and it's yours.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.rights_ready.opt.turnin = Here are the planks.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.cut_offer.text = Set the <b>Sawmill</b> down somewhere flat. Walk up with <b>logs</b> in hand and use the block, and the mill takes them off you. Use it again and you're sawing.\nRun it a while, mill me some lumber, and bring back a stack of <b>planks</b> so I can see your cut.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.cut_offer.opt.accept = I'll get it running.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.grain_offer.text = Every <b>log</b> has more in it than plain boards. The mill knows the decorative <b>cut</b> and the ornate one too, it only wants telling. Crouch as you use the block and it'll ask which.\nMill me some of each, so I know you can read a grain.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.grain_offer.opt.accept = I'll try every cut.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.bench_offer.text = One mill's a start. It's no yard. Put a proper load of lumber through yours, the kind of load that empties a hillside, and bring me the <b>sap</b> it sweats out while you're at it.\nDo that and I'll find you a second <b>Sawmill</b>.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.bench_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring the sap.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_offer.text = You've the hang of planks. Now the other thing.\nOld <b>wood</b> holds something that isn't sap and isn't bark, and a mill with a good hand on it shakes it loose. <b>Essence of Life</b>, the alchemists call it. I call it the fat of the log. Mill till you've a load of it, and bring me a share.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you essence.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_offer.opt.what = What's in the wood?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_ready.text = There it is. <b>Essence of Life</b>, still warm from the cut. Most sawyers go a lifetime and never spot it in the sawdust. Hand it over.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.essence_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the essence.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.edge_offer.text = Short jobs are done. Now a long one.\nStand at that mill for a shift that'd wear out a lesser back, and get your woodcutting up to where I'd call you a sawyer to your face. Nothing to hand in. Come back when it's done and I'll know.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.edge_offer.opt.accept = I'll put the shift in.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.grain_stock_offer.text = Sawyer, and swinging a hatchet any smith could've made. That's been bothering me.\nI'm making you one. My own pattern, and it starts at the haft. Straight grain, no knots, and you don't find that by looking. Put <b>stock</b> through the mill till the yard's full and bring me <b>planks</b>. I'll find the haft in there.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.grain_stock_offer.opt.accept = I'll mill the stock.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.metal_offer.text = That's a haft. Now it wants something on the end of it.\nThe head's cobalt, and cobalt doesn't come out of a log, so for once I'm sending you away from the mill. Find a furnace and bring me <b>Cobalt Ingots</b>. Keep the saw turning while you're gone, mind. A haft with nothing on it is a stick.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.metal_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you cobalt.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.fitting_offer.text = Haft and head. Now they've to be joined, and that's the part nobody hurries.\nThe head's tempered in <b>Essence of Life</b> and the binding's <b>Heavy Leather</b>. Stand at that mill for a long shift, till it's shaking essence loose by the handful, and somewhere in there the deep stuff turns up. Bring me the leather and some <b>Greater Essence of Life</b>, and I'll do the fitting.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.fitting_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring what it needs.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.fitting_ready.text = <b>Heavy Leather</b>, and the <b>Greater Essence of Life</b>. Give them here.\nThere. Cobalt on a straight haft, bound tight enough to outlast the pair of us. It'll not cut like the one the mill hands out, and I'll not pretend it does. It cuts like mine. <color is="#ffd97a">Marn's Hatchet</color>, and there's no other. Take it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.fitting_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the leather and the essence.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.order_ready.text = The day's order. <b>Planks</b> and <b>bark</b>, counted, stacked square. That's how I like a delivery. Same again tomorrow, if you're up for it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.order_ready.opt.turnin = Here's today's order.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trim_ready.text = The trim. <b>Decorative cuts</b>, edges clean, and <b>bark</b> by the armful. Somebody's been reading the grain. There'll be another up before long, if the mill's still standing.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.trim_ready.opt.turnin = Here's today's trim.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.ready_generic.text = You've the look of somebody carrying a finished job. Put it down and we'll settle.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.ready_generic.opt.turnin = Here's what I've done.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.active_generic.text = Still on the job, then. The mill won't run without you standing at it. Go on.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.edge_talk.text = You've a hatchet of mine and a name I don't hand out. There's nothing left in this corner I can make you.\nThe mill's another matter. It's got its own ideas about who it hands an edge to, and standing at it is the only way to find out. There's work here when you want it, same as ever.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.yard_talk.text = Sawyer. That's what I call you now, and I don't say it to many.\nYou've a yard of your own to run. Mine's this corner of the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color>, a long walk from any grove, and it's enough. Come by when you want to talk wood.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.bench_talk.text = You've a mill now. Keep it fed. Planks come first, and the longer you stand at it the more a log gives up. There's work here when you want it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.how_it_works.text = <b>Logs</b> in hand, use the block, and the mill takes them off you. Use it again and you're sawing.\nYour <b>hatchet</b> does the cutting, so a better one means more planks a cycle, and more of everything else the mill turns up in a log, bark to essence. Crouch as you use the block and it'll ask which <b>cut</b> you want.\nThat's the whole of it. The rest is standing there.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.how_it_works.opt.wood = What else is in a log?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.how_it_works.opt.back = Got it.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.what_is_in_wood.text = Bark. Sap. Fiber. Sticks. Every log's got those and the mill throws them off with the sawdust.\nOld wood keeps something else, deeper in, down in the heartwood. Any Kweebec can feel it there before the bark's off. The alchemists boil it down and call it <b>Essence of Life</b>. A steady hand and a good hatchet shake it loose. A clumsy one gets sawdust.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.what_is_in_wood.opt.back = Good to know.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.hatchet_tease.text = There's a <color is="#ffd97a">Sawmiller's Hatchet</color>. Mithril, balanced at the mill, keener than anything a forge puts out. Nobody makes it.\nNow and then a mill hands one to a sawyer who's stood at it long enough with a fine blade already in hand. And I mean now and then. I've seen it happen. Not to me.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.hatchet_tease.opt.back = I'll keep sawing.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.kit_talk.text = That cap I gave you is a start, and I'll not pretend it's more. There's a proper kit.\nWoodcutter's leather, the full set of it. Cap, jerkin, gloves, breeches, all cut for a day at the saw, and nobody sells it. I pay it out of the <b>trim work</b>, a piece now and then when the day's cut is good, and the jerkin comes up least of all. Wear the lot and the mill starts to notice you.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.kit_talk.opt.back = I'll keep at the trim.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.returned = I'm back with what you asked for.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.quests = Anything need cutting?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.how = How does the mill work?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.edge = Ever seen a better edge?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.kit = What goes with this cap?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.nothing = Nothing for now.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.opt.enchanter_who = Who's the priest in the corner?
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.enchanter_intro.text = Him? Outlander, by the robes, and a Kweebec learns to watch those. He's not swung at anybody yet. Orrin, he calls himself. He keeps a table over there that takes gear apart and gives the makings back, and he's been wanting somebody to use it.\nGo on over and say hello. Tell him I sent you. He talks like a book, mind.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.enchanter_intro.opt.accept = I'll go and see him.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.enchanter_intro.opt.back = Maybe later.
dialogue.mmo_sawyer.enchanter_brief.text = He's in the far corner of the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color>, stone at his back and a book in his hand. <color is="#ffd97a">Enchanter Orrin</color>. Say hello and he'll do the rest of the talking.

quest.meet_the_enchanter.title = A Word with Orrin
quest.meet_the_enchanter.flavor = There's a priest in the far corner with a book and a table nobody else will touch. Outlander, by the robes. Harmless, I think. Go and say hello.
quest.the_lesser_table.title = The Lesser Table
quest.the_lesser_table.flavor = I keep a frame for a Disenchanting Table and nothing to finish it with. Bring me Iron Ingots and Essence of Life. It has stood idle long enough.
quest.first_unmaking.title = First Unmaking
quest.first_unmaking.flavor = Set a piece of gear on the table and begin. Watch it come apart. Then bring me a little of the essence it gives up, so I know the rite was done properly.
quest.three_kinds_of_gear.title = Three Kinds of Gear
quest.three_kinds_of_gear.flavor = A sword and a breastplate are not the same thing to the table, and a hatchet is a third thing again. Unmake some of each and you will know what the table knows.
quest.the_essence_draw.title = The Essence Draw
quest.the_essence_draw.flavor = Essence of Life is the wage of this work. Draw a proper measure of it out of gear and bring me a share. I have uses for it that the alchemists do not.
quest.worn_through.title = The Scrap Heap
quest.worn_through.flavor = Gear that is nearly spent still holds something. Take the blades you were about to throw away and the boots you walked through, and sit at the table until they are all gone.
quest.mithril_unmade.title = Mithril Unmade
quest.mithril_unmade.flavor = Mithril is forged with void in it. Every smith knows and none of them say so. Set one mithril piece on the table and watch what comes out of it.
quest.steady_hands.title = Steady Hands
quest.steady_hands.flavor = The rite rewards a practiced hand. Sit at the table for a long while, until you stop flinching when a piece comes apart.
quest.the_greater_table.title = The Greater Table
quest.the_greater_table.flavor = There is a wider table, one that holds three pieces at once and draws deeper. It wants thorium and silk, and Essence of the Void to wake it. Bring me those. I have kept its frame a long time.
quest.shadoweave.title = The Cult's Cloth
quest.shadoweave.flavor = The cult weaves a cloth that drinks the light. I wore it for years. Bring me scraps of it off the Outlanders, unmake the weapons they carry, and I will tell you why I left.
quest.a_thread_of_void.title = A Thread of Void
quest.a_thread_of_void.flavor = Good gear carries a thread of void in it, put there at the forge. The table pulls it loose. Draw some out and bring me a few threads; I keep count of what I take back.
quest.outlander_steel.title = Outlander Steel
quest.outlander_steel.flavor = The Outlanders carry Doomed weapons, forged with more void than any smith should use. Take some from them. Then set the weapons on the table and let it drain them.
quest.the_voidheart.title = The Voidheart
quest.the_voidheart.flavor = A Voidheart is the void given a shape. Work the greater table until you are sure of it, then bring me one heart, from wherever you find it.
quest.iron_for_the_mill.title = Iron for the Mill
quest.iron_for_the_mill.flavor = The sawyer is always short of iron, and I am tired of hearing it. Unmake a few iron hatchets at the table and carry the ore they give back across the landing to him.
quest.a_second_table.title = A Second Table
quest.a_second_table.flavor = A second table can stand wherever you do your work, so you are not forever walking back to the first. Unmake a pile of gear at yours and bring me Essence of Life from the work.
quest.unmaking_rites.title = Unmaking Rites
quest.unmaking_rites.flavor = A few pieces unmade each day, and a tithe of Essence of Life brought to me. I have kept this rite since the night I left the cult. Keep it with me.
quest.loose_threads.title = Loose Threads
quest.loose_threads.flavor = Armor and weapons, unmade in turn, and a tithe of essence. A short order, and it comes round often.
quest.a_weeks_unmaking.title = A Week's Unmaking
quest.a_weeks_unmaking.flavor = A week at the table, counted in pieces and in essence, and a few threads of void brought back to me at the end of it. Clear your evenings.

quest.bounty_quick_unmaking.title = Quick Unmaking
quest.bounty_quick_unmaking.flavor = Somebody is clearing out a cellar full of old gear. Take a few pieces apart at a Disenchanting Table.
quest.bounty_quick_draw.title = Quick Essence
quest.bounty_quick_draw.flavor = Essence of Life, drawn out of old gear at a Disenchanting Table. Essence from a farm is no good for this one.
quest.bounty_table_shift.title = Table Shift
quest.bounty_table_shift.flavor = A short sitting at a Disenchanting Table. Old gear from the bottom of a chest will do.
quest.bounty_essence_tithe.title = Essence Tithe
quest.bounty_essence_tithe.flavor = Essence of Life, handed in here. It does not matter whether a table, a farm or a chest gave it up.
quest.bounty_unmaking_order.title = Unmaking Order
quest.bounty_unmaking_order.flavor = The smiths want their scrap back. Take gear apart at a Disenchanting Table until the order is full.
quest.bounty_void_draw.title = Void Draw
quest.bounty_void_draw.flavor = A buyer wants Essence of the Void drawn at a table and nowhere else. Good gear gives it up.
quest.bounty_mithril_unmaking.title = Mithril Unmaking
quest.bounty_mithril_unmaking.flavor = Mithril gear taken apart at a Disenchanting Table. Crude blades will not count.
quest.bounty_long_unmaking.title = The Long Unmaking
quest.bounty_long_unmaking.flavor = An old armory is being cleared out, every piece of it unmade at a Disenchanting Table. Plan on a long week.
quest.bounty_essence_week.title = Essence in Bulk
quest.bounty_essence_week.flavor = A week's worth of Essence of Life drawn out of gear at a Disenchanting Table. Essence from a farm or the mill is no use here.

